{
  "_doc": "The town's holidays (docs/festivals.md). Every festival here is a proposal, not canon. when.rule: date (month, day), nth_weekday (month, nth 1..5 or -1 last, weekday 0 Monday), easter_orthodox / easter_western (offset days from Easter Sunday), weekly (weekdays, months), trigger (the game fires it: first_snow); offset shifts any rule's day. days: how long it lasts. holiday: offices and schools close (holiday_days: which of its days, default all). decor: from/to hours (from 00:00 of the first day; negative = the day before; to counted from the last day, may pass 24), kinds (bunting, flags, lanterns, stage, stalls, tree, wreaths, candles, birdhouses), venues (default: the program's). program: phases with hours [from, to) from 00:00 of their day (may pass 24), day (0 first, -1 every day), venue (a spot kind or id of the city plan: square, fair, beach, pier, promenade, park, sunrise_point), mode (how people take part: mingle, watch, sit, fair), pull (0..2, how strongly it draws people), face (what watchers look at: stage, sea, bonfire, tree, sky, sunrise), show (what the game puts on: music, stage_lights, fireworks, sky_lanterns, bonfire, meteors). priority: who has a venue when two festivals want it at once.",
